{"iter_dir": "iter-003-m1-basis-form-fpu-q", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T03:30:00+00:00", "verdict": "REJECT", "action": "reverted", "kernel_ms_median": 97.545, "kernel_ms_p99": 102.6439, "per_view_median": {"hero": 97.545, "side": 88.525, "top": 102.38}, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": 43.90745857563266, "side": 46.8968312224647, "top": 41.81050878351938}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "044f398", "high_promotion_priority": false, "correction": "Original KEEP verdict overrode the validator subagent's REJECT call on diff10 cross-hatch. User-flagged regression at the bottom of Stitch's ears in hero.png. Basis-form Q has catastrophic cancellation (6 fp32 terms of magnitude ~10 summed to a small result), and per-tile bf16 packing of R/G/B/T state accumulates divergent error patterns across tile boundaries. Reverted in 044f398; baseline restored by iter-005 verification."}
{"iter_dir": "iter-004-fuse-inner-acquires", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T03:30:01+00:00", "verdict": "REJECT", "action": "reverted", "kernel_ms_median": 99.67, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": 43.9, "side": 46.9, "top": 41.8}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "044f398", "high_promotion_priority": false, "correction": "Never reached verdict \u2014 built on iter-003 M1 (inherits tile-seam artifact). Rolled back as part of M1 revert. Timing 99.67 ms regressed from prev_best 97.55 ms; the SFPU DST-DST fusions were slower than the prior FPU mul_tiles."}
{"iter_dir": "iter-005-verify-revert-baseline", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T03:30:02+00:00", "verdict": "KEEP", "action": "no_commit_baseline_reproduced", "kernel_ms_median": 100.335, "kernel_ms_p99": 105.7213, "per_view_median": {"hero": 100.335, "side": 90.86, "top": 105.6}, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": Infinity, "side": Infinity, "top": Infinity}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "f50be70", "high_promotion_priority": false}
{"iter_dir": "iter-006-d1-fuse-contrib", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T04:00:00+00:00", "verdict": "REJECT", "action": "revert", "kernel_ms_median": 100.695, "kernel_ms_p99": 106.2368, "per_view_median": {"hero": 100.695, "side": 91.225, "top": 106.085}, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": Infinity, "side": Infinity, "top": Infinity}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "dc1b6d5", "high_promotion_priority": false, "lesson": "SFPU mul_binary_tile (DST-DST) costs more than the acquire/commit/wait/release + CB_T_TMP reserve/pack/push/wait/pop roundtrip it saves. Bit-identical (PSNR \u221e, diff10 black) but kernel ms regressed 99.95 \u2192 100.69. Don't use SFPU DST-DST as a perf fusion. Next: try FPU binary_dest_reuse_tiles<ELWMUL, DEST_TO_SRCA> for same fusion."}
{"iter_dir": "iter-007-d1-fuse-fpu", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T03:40:07.326363+00:00", "verdict": "KEEP", "action": "commit", "kernel_ms_median": 99.34, "kernel_ms_p99": 104.7039, "per_view_median": {"hero": 99.34, "side": 89.985, "top": 104.515}, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": 59.51822203462508, "side": 62.26025128398001, "top": 59.9949490355364}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "5a4e19a4c20641365ef08cd0e4f756a25e10589a", "high_promotion_priority": false}
{"iter_dir": "iter-008-d2-fuse-fpu", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T04:30:00+00:00", "verdict": "REJECT", "action": "revert", "kernel_ms_median": null, "psnr_per_view": null, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "02c8089", "high_promotion_priority": false, "failure_mode": "kernel_deadlock_or_device_contention", "lesson": "Render daemon hung within cycle 1; no per-cycle timing line emitted. ORIGINAL HYPOTHESIS: per-channel D2 fuse (copy_tile + mul_unary_tile + binary_dest_reuse_tiles<ELWADD, DEST_TO_SRCA>) deadlocks via SFPU/FPU mixed chain through binary_dest_reuse_tiles. CORRECTION: after iter-009, discovered that the dev viewer's daemon holds /dev/tenstorrent/0 silently \u2014 concurrent dispatches just hang. The iter-008 hang may have been device contention, not a real kernel bug. Status: untested. Re-run only after killing all device-holding processes. Until proven, treat SFPU/FPU mixed chains across binary_dest_reuse_tiles as suspect (matches the M2 86c5ae2 deadlock pattern), but the iter-008 result alone is no longer conclusive evidence."}
{"iter_dir": "iter-009-b2-fuse-fpu", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T05:30:52.827336+00:00", "verdict": "REJECT", "action": "revert", "kernel_ms_median": 100.695, "kernel_ms_p99": 106.1726, "per_view_median": {"hero": 100.695, "side": 91.18, "top": 105.81}, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": 59.51822203462508, "side": 62.26025128398001, "top": 59.9949490355364}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "f7bf6a1", "high_promotion_priority": false, "lesson": "Collapsing 3 FPU mul_tiles (dx\u00b2/dy\u00b2/dx\u00b7dy) into one acquire regressed kernel ms 99.34 \u2192 100.70 (+1.37%) while producing bit-identical output. Same negative result as iter-006: removing acquire cycles for FPU ops eliminates overlap between pack and the next stage's setup. The 3 muls run serially inside one acquire and pack waits at tile_regs_release. Three explicit acquires let pack overlap with the next setup. Lesson: don't fuse independent FPU ops into one acquire just to save acquire/commit/wait/release cycles \u2014 the pack/setup overlap is more valuable than the cycles saved.", "stage_medians": {"total_ms": 324.66759000817547, "project_ms": 17.032228992320597, "tile_assign_ms": 11.045532497519162, "sort_ms": 67.05086099100299, "blend_ms": 228.3610840095207}}
{"iter_dir": "iter-010-e-fuse-fpu", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T05:44:08.813644+00:00", "verdict": "KEEP", "action": "commit", "kernel_ms_median": 97.77, "kernel_ms_p99": 103.0971, "per_view_median": {"hero": 97.77, "side": 88.71000000000001, "top": 102.905}, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": 40.40181099360784, "side": 43.69705259506113, "top": 40.149730293255274}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "e893fb11f2f09c114b3f07789ac2bb322d9f89d2", "high_promotion_priority": false, "stage_medians": {"total_ms": 315.88849849504186, "project_ms": 16.48248900892213, "tile_assign_ms": 10.3000035014702, "sort_ms": 65.61999700352317, "blend_ms": 222.96079149964498}}
{"iter_dir": "iter-011-b3b-fuse-fpu", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T05:50:05.449730+00:00", "verdict": "NEEDS_REVIEW", "action": "revert", "kernel_ms_median": 97.9, "kernel_ms_p99": 102.9371, "per_view_median": {"hero": 97.9, "side": 88.715, "top": 102.85499999999999}, "psnr_per_view": {"hero": 39.69374661393664, "side": 43.066736097074596, "top": 38.86972289570602}, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "48411e0", "high_promotion_priority": false, "lesson": "Stacking two binary_dest_reuse<ELWADD, DEST_TO_SRCA> applications in one acquire (add_tiles + binary_dest_reuse on CB_Q) drops PSNR ~1 dB further than a single application. Combined with iter-007's and iter-010's ~1 dB drops each, hero went 40.40 \u2192 39.69 and top 40.15 \u2192 38.87 \u2014 both below the 40 dB kernel-algebra floor. AND kernel ms 97.77 \u2192 97.90 (+0.13%, break-even within noise). DEST_TO_SRCA reload appears to truncate to bf16 between ops; pure pack/unpack roundtrips preserve precision better. Budget remaining binary_dest_reuse applications carefully \u2014 we can afford at most 1-2 more before the 35 dB hard floor. Pick big-acquire-savings fusions only.", "stage_medians": {"total_ms": 321.516606505611, "project_ms": 16.85569049732294, "tile_assign_ms": 11.649738502455875, "sort_ms": 67.04450550023466, "blend_ms": 225.5764250003267}}
{"iter_dir": "iter-012-init-fuse", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T06:45:00+00:00", "verdict": "REJECT", "action": "revert", "kernel_ms_median": null, "psnr_per_view": null, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "3395f56", "high_promotion_priority": false, "failure_mode": "kernel_deadlock", "lesson": "Multi-slot fill_tile in one acquire deadlocks the kernel. Two variants tried: (A) pack_tile(3, CB_T_STATE) + pack_tile(3, CB_SAT_MASK) reusing same dst slot \u2014 hang. (B) 2-acquire form: fill_tile(0..3) for R/G/B/T then fill_tile(0) for SAT_MASK \u2014 also hang. Both blocked daemon in futex_wait_queue_me holding /dev/tenstorrent/0. No working multi-slot fill_tile precedent in tt-metal programming_examples or tests. fill_tile.h says idst is unconstrained, but in practice the SFPU fill pipeline appears to require single-slot use. For per-tile state init, stick with the original 5-acquire pattern OR use copy_tile from a pre-populated CB_CONST tile. Don't try multi-slot fill_tile again without a tt-metal reference example."}
{"iter_dir": "iter-013-drop-stage-e-sat-mask", "timestamp": "2026-05-26T07:30:00+00:00", "verdict": "REJECT", "action": "revert", "kernel_ms_median": null, "psnr_per_view": null, "class": "kernel-algebra", "commit_sha": "d76710a", "high_promotion_priority": false, "failure_mode": "kernel_deadlock", "lesson": "Removing binary_dest_reuse<ELWMUL, DEST_TO_SRCA>(CB_SAT_MASK) from iter-010's fused acquire deadlocks the kernel. Two attempts (one on dirty device, one with fresh JIT cache + verified clean device) both hung at cycle 1 within 5 min. The mul_tiles \u2192 binary_dest_reuse \u2192 pack triad is not freely reversible: pack_tile appears to depend on internal pipeline state established by binary_dest_reuse_tiles_init, even though it nominally reads from dst[0] which holds the mul_tiles result. Lesson: to recover PSNR headroom from iter-007/iter-010 fusions, the *whole triad* must be reverted to a 2-acquire form, not just the binary_dest_reuse half. Plan doc preserved in iter-013-drop-stage-e-sat-mask.md."}
